WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.880
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going&nbsp;
to explain an American comedy-drama film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:15.920
called “An American Pickle.” Spoilers&nbsp;
ahead! Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:22.160
The movie begins in the year 1919 in a&nbsp;
place called shtetl in Eastern Europe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.640
Herschel Greenbaum is a struggling Jewish&nbsp;
laborer who works as a ditch digger.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:32.400
His job is tiresome and makes him little to no&nbsp;
money. Most of the money he earns, he spends on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:37.520
buying new shovels which break frequently.&nbsp;
Herschel narrates that his life is tough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:44.080
but that was until he saw the love of his life,&nbsp;
Sarah for the first time. By buying her a golden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:49.440
fish from the market, he wins her over and the&nbsp;
two become friends. They have a lot in common,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.160
like the fact that both their parents were&nbsp;
murdered by Russian Cossacks. The pair’s greatest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.160 --> 00:01:04.080
wish is to be able to afford their own gravestone&nbsp;
one day. A few months later, they get married,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:09.520
hoping for a peaceful life together. However,&nbsp;
their plans are ruined when the Russian Cossacks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.880
attack the village right after the wedding&nbsp;
ceremony. To escape the life of living in fear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.840
the couple moves to America. They are frequently&nbsp;
called antisemitic slang but Herschel claims&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:24.960
that the Americans treat them way better than&nbsp;
Russians did. He gets a job at a pickle factory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:30.640
where he earns a nickel for every ten rats he&nbsp;
kills. The couple works hard and finally buys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:36.400
two graves to be together even after death.
Not long after, Sarah gets pregnant with their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:42.320
first child. But everything changes when one&nbsp;
day, Herschel falls into a vat of pickles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:48.480
just as the factory is closed for health reasons.&nbsp;
The vat is covered, and he is stuck inside it for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:54.960
the next one hundred years. Time passes but no&nbsp;
one comes to look for him. Until two youngsters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.760
enter the factory and open the vat’s lid that&nbsp;
was accidentally knocked out by their drone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:07.200
Even after a hundred years of being stuck inside&nbsp;
it, Herschel is alive and well. His story becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:11.920
the talk of the city and a convention is&nbsp;
held to explain how he was able to survive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:16.560
The scientists provide a very believable&nbsp;
explanation which the media accepts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:21.440
Following that, Herschel is taken to the hospital&nbsp;
for a check-up and is found to be in perfectly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:27.040
good condition except for his anger issues. On&nbsp;
running a background check, the doctors find out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:32.960
that all of Herschel’s descendants are dead except&nbsp;
for his great-grandson, Ben. After they contact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:38.000
him, they find out he lives in Brooklyn and is&nbsp;
more than happy to pick up his great grandfather.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:50.000
Ben meets Herschel and is surprised to see that&nbsp;
the two look almost identical. When Herschel steps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.600
out of the building for the first time, he is&nbsp;
mesmerized by the skyscrapers and the vehicles.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.600 --> 00:03:00.640
Everything has changed since he last saw New&nbsp;
York. Ben is excited to be able to show his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:05.600
great grandfather all the new inventions. 
When they reach Ben’s apartment, Herschel is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:10.960
even more shocked. Used to living in poverty, he&nbsp;
thinks that the place is massive and luxurious.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:21.280
Ben welcomes him to live there as long as he wants&nbsp;
but Herschel thoughtfully says he doesn’t want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:26.480
be a burden on him. Herschel’s excitement only&nbsp;
gets bigger when he gets to drink Seltzer water,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:32.880
a drink that was reserved for royalties in his&nbsp;
time. Ben makes Alexa play an old song and the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:38.640
dance together. After settling down, Herschel asks&nbsp;
Ben what he does for work, assuming that he might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:45.200
be a doctor or a lawyer. He is visibly confused&nbsp;
when Ben says he is a freelance app developer. Ben&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:50.800
explains that he has been developing an app called&nbsp;
"Boop Bop'', for the past five years and is very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:57.440
passionate about it. It is a service that checks&nbsp;
companies' ethics when buying their products.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:03.280
Herschel sees no pictures of the family on the&nbsp;
walls, so he asks Ben about it. Ben shows him a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:09.120
family photo album which gets Herschel emotional.&nbsp;
He sees Sarah’s picture and finds out that he had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:15.840
a son. On being asked about his parents, Ben gets&nbsp;
uncomfortable. He says that they passed away in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:21.840
an accident. The next day, they go to visit the&nbsp;
graves of their family and to Herschel’s horror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:27.840
the cemetery is in shambles. Seeing his wife’s&nbsp;
poorly kept tombstone, he can't help but cry. 
&nbsp;

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:34.400
Some workers are putting up a billboard of Russian&nbsp;
vodka right on top of their graves. This reminds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:40.480
Herschel of the Cossacks who killed his parents&nbsp;
and loved ones back in Shtetl. An enraged Herschel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:46.720
asks them to put it down but they do not oblige,&nbsp;
making him assault them. Ben tries to stop him but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:52.640
gets beaten up instead. This results in both of&nbsp;
them being arrested. Ben spends a large sum of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.640 --> 00:05:01.677
money and bails them out. That day, Ben goes to a&nbsp;
meeting with an investor who is willing to invest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.677 --> 00:05:06.960
in his app. But he is devastated to find out that&nbsp;
the investors have dropped him because of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:12.960
criminal report. He returns home and blames&nbsp;
Herschel for making his life go downhill.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:18.160
Herschel doesn’t understand Ben’s ideas and claims&nbsp;
that they should start a pickle business instead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:24.320
In a fit of rage, Ben says that Sarah would be&nbsp;
ashamed of him if she were alive. At that moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:30.720
Herschel vows to build a pickle empire and make&nbsp;
his dead relatives proud by cutting down the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:36.400
billboard. He storms out of the apartment after&nbsp;
calling Ben a dishonor to their family name. 
&nbsp;

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:41.360
At first, he goes to the grocery store to buy&nbsp;
cucumbers but they are too expensive. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:47.440
wandering around, he notices that the bin outside&nbsp;
of the store has packed cucumbers in it. He brings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:52.240
them with him and in a similar fashion, collects&nbsp;
all the necessary ingredients from dumpsters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:58.240
around the city. Using a shopping cart, salt, and&nbsp;
rainwater, he is able to finally make the brine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:03.280
for the pickles. Following that, he puts up&nbsp;
a tiny pickle stand by the side of the road.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:08.560
He sells his first jar for four dollars to a&nbsp;
couple. Since he hasn’t added any preservatives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:12.720
and is selling them at a lower price than&nbsp;
the grocery store, the number of customers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:17.840
increases. He also asks them to bring the jars&nbsp;
back after they are finished, this way the people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:23.200
believe his business is environment friendly.&nbsp;
His customers start to post him on social media&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:32.240
which grows his business exponentially. Soon, Ben&nbsp;
finds out about Herschel’s local pickle business&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:36.720
that everyone is talking about. While he&nbsp;
struggles to create ideas for his new app,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:41.680
he is told that Herschel’s business is a&nbsp;
massive hit. This gets him jealous. 
&nbsp;

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:46.640
One day, he calls the health department and&nbsp;
files a complaint about Herschel using products&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:51.840
found in the trash bins to create his pickles.&nbsp;
This causes his business to shut down and he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:58.240
is fined $12,000. Herschel is left right where he&nbsp;
started without any resources. Two of his faithful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:03.360
customers advise him to hire interns since he&nbsp;
wouldn’t have to pay them. Herschel is inspired&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:13.760
by the idea, even though he thinks it is similar&nbsp;
to slavery. He hires a group of interns to brine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:19.520
and package the pickles. Soon, they use proper&nbsp;
ethical methods to make them and are approved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:24.720
by the health department. The interns also help&nbsp;
him sell the pickle on a larger scale making the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:30.240
business quickly go back up. In no time, Herschel&nbsp;
earns enough money to purchase the billboard and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:35.440
take it down. In the meantime, Ben sees that the&nbsp;
people who were supposed to invest in his app&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:40.400
are now wanting to invest in Herschel’s business.&nbsp;
To proclaim his victory, Herschel brings the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:45.520
billboard back to Ben’s apartment. He says that he&nbsp;
wants to help Ben because, at the end of the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:52.000
they are family. But Ben is not fond of the idea&nbsp;
and just wants the man to go away. As they chat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:57.840
Herschel comments how the Polish men are stupid.&nbsp;
This gives Ben another idea on how he can end the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:03.440
pickle business; he suggests Herschel create a&nbsp;
Twitter account. That evening, with an intern’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:08.880
help, Herschel tweets controversial statements&nbsp;
about women, religion, and homosexuality. 
&nbsp;

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:13.600
The following day, people swarm before&nbsp;
his shop and protest against his ideas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:18.800
urging everyone to boycott his pickle business.&nbsp;
His interns also leave his side and join&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:24.560
the protestors. Even after that, Herschel&nbsp;
stays firm in his opinions. As time passes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:30.320
he earns support from conservative groups who see&nbsp;
him as an icon of free speech and empowerment. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:35.680
even gets selected to appear for a debate with&nbsp;
a college professor on the subject of ethics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:41.200
At first, his statements about women, in general,&nbsp;
are seen as bold opinions. But then, a disguised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:46.400
Ben from the audience, asks him about his thoughts&nbsp;
on Christianity. Herschel proceeds to say that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:51.920
Virgin Mary invented Christianity to hide the fact&nbsp;
that she had sexual relations. He calls everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:57.280
who believes in Jesus, an idiot. Because of the&nbsp;
comment, the people who were on his side till now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:02.320
chase him down the streets of New York, wanting&nbsp;
to kill him for disrespecting their religion. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:07.920
manages to save his life by hiding in an alleyway.&nbsp;
At night, he sees a news report about protests&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:14.240
happening all across America to boycott him once&nbsp;
and for all. Authorities start to dig up his past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:19.440
wanting to deport him back to Eastern Europe.&nbsp;
Moreover, because of the outdated filing system&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:24.080
in the storage facility, the paperwork&nbsp;
for Herschel’s arrival cannot be located.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:28.560
This gives the authorities an excuse to&nbsp;
revoke his citizenship. He is declared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:34.320
a fugitive illegal alien and the people are&nbsp;
asked to report the police if they see him. 
&nbsp;

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:40.560
With no way out, Herschel goes to his only family,&nbsp;
Ben for help. Not wanting to return to Shtetl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:45.440
he says that he will move to Canada and start a&nbsp;
business there. Ben reluctantly agrees to help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:51.120
him for the last time. The two drive to Canadian&nbsp;
borders and walk through the woods to illegally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:56.480
enter the country. On their way, Ben accidentally&nbsp;
cuts his palm, and Herschel tears a piece of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.480 --> 00:10:01.760
clothes to bandage the wound. At night, he&nbsp;
hugs his great-grandson to keep him warm.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:07.520
Although Ben has said vicious things to him,&nbsp;
Herschel considers him family. The next morning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:12.400
they finally reach the border but have to hide&nbsp;
when they are almost spotted by border patrol.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:16.960
While chatting, Ben feels bad for Herschel&nbsp;
and confesses that he was the one who asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:21.680
him the question about Christianity because&nbsp;
he wanted to sabotage the pickle business.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:26.800
Ben hopes that Herschel will forgive him but&nbsp;
he is punched in the face instead. He falls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:32.080
unconscious and the commotion attracts the border&nbsp;
patrol’s attention. Herschel hides and finds Ben’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:39.360
razor and clothes in a bag. He quickly thinks of&nbsp;
a way to escape and disguises himself as Ben. 
&nbsp;

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:45.280
The officers arrest Ben, thinking he is Herschel&nbsp;
while Herschel, himself is let free because he has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:50.800
Ben’s ID. Following that, Ben is put on trial but&nbsp;
his case is considered a joke when he pleads that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:56.080
he is not Herschel. Eventually, he is sent to&nbsp;
Shtetl instead of his great grandfather. He is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.080 --> 00:11:01.680
alone and cold in a town filled with strangers who&nbsp;
do not speak English. He tries to talk to people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:06.560
asking them for a place he can spend the night&nbsp;
in. He ends up in a synagogue and decides to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:12.640
stay there. Meanwhile, Herschel feels awful for&nbsp;
his great-grandson. He goes to his apartment and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:16.800
looks through the family photo album. While&nbsp;
reminiscing about the old days, he finds a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:22.720
drawing that Ben had made of his parents as a kid.&nbsp;
It is only then, that Herschel finds out Boop and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:28.720
Bop were pet names that Ben gave his parents. He&nbsp;
realizes that Ben had always wanted to honor his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:34.400
parents and feels terrible that he misjudged him.&nbsp;
Following that, the man decides to go to Shtetl&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:40.240
and bring Ben back home. Meanwhile, in Shtetl,&nbsp;
Ben is called by the people of the synagogue to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:46.160
perform prayer and pay respect to the dead family&nbsp;
members. He gets emotional during the prayer but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:51.440
it makes him feel a lot lighter afterward. To&nbsp;
his surprise, Herschel appears in front of him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:57.120
and apologizes for his actions. He says that Ben&nbsp;
is exactly what he wanted his descendants to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.120 --> 00:12:01.840
and claims his parents must be proud&nbsp;
of him. The pair reconcile and go by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:07.280
a lake that used to be Sarah’s favorite spot.
They discuss starting a pickle business together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:11.200
where they can pickle more than just&nbsp;
cucumbers. Ben offers to create a website&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:16.560
for their company through which they can sell&nbsp;
worldwide. The two finally return to Brooklyn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:21.360
and pay a visit to Sarah’s grave. In the&nbsp;
final scene, they pray together in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:25.600
honor of the dead family members.
